 "_note": "Which model, how many turns and which tools each worker role gets when scripts/run-job.mjs starts it. Haiku for sorting and mechanical checks, Sonnet for research, review and writing, Opus only where judgment errors are costly. The improver job may move a role one tier or max_turns by at most a quarter a day within the bounds in scripts/improve.mjs; roles listed in min_tier never drop below it. Every worker is denied git and file deletion; tools are the smallest set the role needs. Owner, 2026-11-21 (accuracy first: the second review corrected 34% of events against a target under 10%): Opus where it counts, as a routing rule, not a global switch. researcher-deep, updater-deep and followup-deep are the same jobs as researcher, updater and followup (same prompts) on Opus; scripts/lib/routing.mjs sends incidents, exploited flaws, official reports and stories two or more publishers carry to researcher-deep, and severity 3 or exploited events to updater-deep and followup-deep; routine work stays on the base roles (Sonnet). Reviewers stay on Sonnet: `node scripts/review.mjs errors` counts corrections by the role and model that wrote the event, so the owner can see whether the writer or the reviewer is the weak point. Deleting a deep role sends its work back to the base role.",
